  "gradeRuleDescribe": {
    "yms_year": 114.0,
    "yms_smester": 1.0,
    "cls_id": "CE24310",
    "sub_id": "61482",
    "scr_dup": "001",
    "tpa_score_new": "<div>(1) Skill Practice and homwork: 30 % (2) Midterm exam: 30 % (3) Final oral presentation for LCA project: 40%</div>\n",
    "tpa_score_new_en": "(1) Skill Practice and homwork: 30 %\n(2) Midterm exam: 30 % \n(3) Term paper and final oral presentation: 40%",
    "course_pol": "一、課堂禮儀\n1. 請準時到課。\n2. 若需身體不適，請依規定請假。遲到或提早離開時亦同。\n3. 上課會使用手機互動，請攜帶手機。但不可做與課程無關之活動。\n二、課程交流及網路禮儀\n1. 教學與學習以o365信箱作為師生教學與學習溝通之共通工具，並定期檢視信箱。\n2. 您的電子郵件要署名，我不會回覆“匿名”信件。\n3. 任何時間都可以透過ilearn或Teams傳訊息給我，我會盡快回覆。\n4. 電子郵件、公告欄等交流時，要寫清楚資訊，保持禮貌。",
    "course_pol_en": "Classroom Etiquette\n1. Please arrive on time for class.\n2. If you are physically unwell, please take leave as per regulations. The same applies for late arrivals or early departures.\n3. Mobile phones will be used for in-class interactions, so please bring your phone. However, you cannot engage in activities unrelated to the course.\nII. Course Interaction and Online Etiquette\n1. Teaching and learning will use the o365 email as the common tool for teacher-student communication, and the email should be checked regularly.\n2. Your email must be signed, as I will not reply to \"anonymous\" emails.\n3. You can send me messages through ilearn or Teams at any time, and I will respond as soon as possible.\n4. When communicating through email, bulletin boards, etc., provide clear information and maintain politeness.",
    "course_rem": null,
    "course_rem_en": null,
    "ais_meno": "<div>學習必須以誠信為基礎，任何學生企圖將自己未製作的作品，作為自己的作品，此行為是為不誠實行為。在作業、測驗或考試中作弊或抄襲的學生或協助他人的行為，該次成績以零分計，若是累犯，將依逢甲大學學生獎懲辦法提送。</div>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>考核時如果您抄襲他人的答案、或交作業時您交出全部或部分由他人撰寫的論文或作業，則被視為作弊。</li>\n</ul>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>如果您從書本、書報、期刊論文或其他來源，複製材料而沒有識別和確認這些來源，或者是在沒有確認這些來源的情況下抄寫想法，則犯有抄襲或故意竊取的行為。</li>\n</ul>\n",
    "ais_meno_en": "<div>Learning must be based on integrity. Any student attempting to present work that they did not create as their own is an act of dishonesty. Students who cheat or plagiarize on assignments, tests, or exams, or assist others in doing so, will receive a score of zero for that work. Repeat offenders will be subject to disciplinary action in accordance with Feng Chia University&#39;s student reward and punishment regulations.<br />\nCheating during assessments, such as copying answers from others or submitting all or part of a paper or assignment written by someone else, is considered academic dishonesty.<br />\nCopying material from books, newspapers, journal articles, or other sources without properly identifying and acknowledging those sources, or paraphrasing ideas without confirming the sources, constitutes plagiarism or intentional theft.</div>\n",
    "ilearn_mk": null
  },
